{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1183491-what-will-tc-adventure-have","id":1183491,"title":"What will TC: Adventure! have?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-07T23:30:43-08:00","id":1183491,"title":"What will TC: Adventure! have?","content":"TC will provide rules for Talents.<br /> TC: Aeon will provide rules for Psions.<br /> TC: Aberrant will provide rules for Novas.<br /> <br /> What will TC: Adventure provide?<br /> <br /> My guess: Psiads (a.k.a. mesmerists) and \u201cStealth Novas\u201d (a.k.a. stalwarts: a stripped-down version of Novas without overt Quantum Powers, just the 2e equivalent of Enhancements). Presumably with enough mechanics that you won't need to own TC: Aeon to play a mesmerist or TC: Aberrant to play a stalwart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T23:49:02-08:00","id":1183495,"title":"","content":"It's been said that Adventure! will feature lower power versions of Paramorphs, Psychomorphs, and Eximorphs. So yeah, Daredevils, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts seem to be coming back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T01:52:18-08:00","id":1183516,"title":"","content":"I guess what I'm asking is whether TC:Adventure!'s daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts will share a common ruleset as they did in the TU, or if (e.g.) mesmerist powers will be organized into Aptitudes and Modes and fueled by Psi as they are in TC:Aeon. That is, will TC:Adventure! tell us to use slightly tweaked versions of the Talents rules to handle mesmerists and stalwarts, or will it use low-powered versions of the psi and nova rules, respectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</